    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0104" n="62" xml:id="pg62"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 29</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    ECA message files, FRC 53A278, Paris: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting United States Special Representative in
                        Europe (</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Riddleberger</hi><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >) to the Acting Administrator for Economic Cooperation (</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Bissell</hi><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-31T19:00:00+01:00">October 31, 1951—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Repto 5477. For Harriman, Bissell and
                        Porter from Tasca and Gordon. Ref: Torep 8159;<anchor n="1" xml:id="d29-f1"/>
                    Repto 5428;<anchor n="2" xml:id="d29-f2"/>
                    airgram Repto circular A–708.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d29-f3"/> Full text decision OEEC
                    council sent Washington via ref airgram. That plus reftel gives all info available present time. Character of European
                    members will depend in part upon US selection. Role of
                        Stikker in coal plus his two advisers for purpose of
                    supplying political tone required. Steel and power require more high level
                    technical appraisal. Would appear feasible to extend
                        Stikker approach to steel and power on same basis as
                    coal.</p>
                <p>Do not understand reference to high level admin officials. Believe maximum impact
                    US would be thru highly qualified people from industries concerned. Role of US
                    participants would be to supply technical know-how at high level with particular
                    reference to problems of expansion in sectors involved as well as to underline
                    great US interest in development of concrete expansion targets. Incidentally
                    believe that there should be high level labor participation at all stages.
                    Cruikshank considering problem this end.</p>
                <p>Determination of procedure for manpower clearly linked to arrangements made in
                    other fields. In any case, feel further study necessary on our part to determine
                    objectives and suitable procedures to realize objectives. OSR Labor Division currently studying this problem.
                    Believe agriculture would be handled by ordinary vertical Food and Agriculture
                    Comite of OEEC. Urge strongly that you proceed
                    immed with respect to coal, steel and power as recommended Repto 5428. Separate comments will follow on
                    manpower and agriculture. [Tasca and Gordon.]<anchor n="4" xml:id="d29-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Riddleberger</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
